IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-art8-register`
IMPORT `g3-art9-restricted-section`
IMPORT `g3-fixtures`

-- g3-tests-art9-restricted-section.l4: tests of Article 9 (src:254-286).  Expected values are decided from the text before the code was run.
-- The Order under Article 9 is not among the sources: its content is an input everywhere below.

§ `Tests of Article 9: the restricted section`

fav MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`

§§ `Article 9(1): the public elements of the restricted section`

`element (a)` MEANS `the registration number, but not the registered name`
`element (b) status` MEANS `the note of status registered under Article 8(3)(a)`
`element (b) purposes` MEANS `the registered charitable purposes registered under Article 8(3)(e)`
`element (b) benefit` MEANS `the registered public benefit statement registered under Article 8(3)(f)`
`element (b) annual return` MEANS `the note of the annual return registered under Article 8(3)(j)`
`element (b) notice` MEANS `the note of a required steps notice registered under Article 8(3)(k)`
`element (c)` MEANS `a summary of the reasons for registration in the restricted section`
`element (d)` MEANS `another element prescribed by the Minister by Order`

GIVEN summary IS A BOOLEAN
      prescribed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for the public elements (Article 9(1))`
`element facts: summary produced` summary `, an Order prescribes another element` prescribed MEANS
    `Facts for the public elements (Article 9(1))` WITH
        `a summary of the reasons has been produced by the charity to the satisfaction of the Commissioner` IS summary
        `an Order under Article 9(1)(d) prescribes another element` IS prescribed

`a notice served on the charity, complied with` MEANS
    `Required steps notice` WITH
        `served on` IS `the registered charity`
        `prompted by` IS `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`
        `date served` IS YMD 2024 1 10
        `steps to be taken by` IS NOTHING
        `requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS FALSE
        `has been complied with` IS TRUE

`a notice served on a governor, not complied with` MEANS
    `Required steps notice` WITH
        `served on` IS `a governor of the registered charity`
        `prompted by` IS `a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct`
        `date served` IS YMD 2025 3 5
        `steps to be taken by` IS NOTHING
        `requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS FALSE
        `has been complied with` IS FALSE

-- A charity in the restricted section, with a summary and no notice: the number, the four matters that are always registered, and the summary -- not the name.
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the public elements of the restricted section` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and entered in the restricted section` EMPTY (`element facts: summary produced` TRUE `, an Order prescribes another element` FALSE) EQUALS LIST `element (a)`, `element (b) status`, `element (b) purposes`, `element (b) benefit`, `element (b) annual return`, `element (c)`
-- Without a summary produced to the Commissioner's satisfaction, no element (c).
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the public elements of the restricted section` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and entered in the restricted section` EMPTY (`element facts: summary produced` FALSE `, an Order prescribes another element` FALSE) EQUALS LIST `element (a)`, `element (b) status`, `element (b) purposes`, `element (b) benefit`, `element (b) annual return`
-- A notice served: the note of it is a public element.
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the public elements of the restricted section` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and entered in the restricted section` (LIST `a notice served on a governor, not complied with`) (`element facts: summary produced` FALSE `, an Order prescribes another element` FALSE) EQUALS LIST `element (a)`, `element (b) status`, `element (b) purposes`, `element (b) benefit`, `element (b) annual return`, `element (b) notice`
-- Another element an Order prescribes (9(1)(d)).
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the public elements of the restricted section` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and entered in the restricted section` EMPTY (`element facts: summary produced` FALSE `, an Order prescribes another element` TRUE) EQUALS LIST `element (a)`, `element (b) status`, `element (b) purposes`, `element (b) benefit`, `element (b) annual return`, `element (d)`
-- All eight.
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the public elements of the restricted section` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and entered in the restricted section` (LIST `a notice served on a governor, not complied with`) (`element facts: summary produced` TRUE `, an Order prescribes another element` TRUE) EQUALS LIST `element (a)`, `element (b) status`, `element (b) purposes`, `element (b) benefit`, `element (b) annual return`, `element (b) notice`, `element (c)`, `element (d)`
-- F3.8: a notice complied with is noted on the favoured reading and not on the other.
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the public elements of the restricted section` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and entered in the restricted section` (LIST `a notice served on the charity, complied with`) (`element facts: summary produced` FALSE `, an Order prescribes another element` FALSE) EQUALS LIST `element (a)`, `element (b) status`, `element (b) purposes`, `element (b) benefit`, `element (b) annual return`, `element (b) notice`
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the public elements of the restricted section` `interpretation F3.8 reading B` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and entered in the restricted section` (LIST `a notice served on the charity, complied with`) (`element facts: summary produced` FALSE `, an Order prescribes another element` FALSE) EQUALS LIST `element (a)`, `element (b) status`, `element (b) purposes`, `element (b) benefit`, `element (b) annual return`
-- "in relation to each charity registered in that section": no element for a charity in any other section.
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the public elements of the restricted section` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` EMPTY (`element facts: summary produced` TRUE `, an Order prescribes another element` TRUE) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the public elements of the restricted section` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and deregistered on 1 June 2024` EMPTY (`element facts: summary produced` TRUE `, an Order prescribes another element` TRUE) EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `Article 9(1): is a given matter one of the public elements?`

-- (a): the registration number, "but not the registered name".
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` `the registration number`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` `the registered name`
-- (b): the matters registered under 8(3)(a), (e), (f), (j) and (k), and no other.
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `a note of the status of the entity`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the names of each of the governors`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the principal address`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the address of any other premises in Jersey`)
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the registered charitable purposes`)
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the registered public benefit statement`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the date on which the charity was registered`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `a note that the charity is an organized religious charity`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the text of the provision in the constitution that falls within Article 5(2)`)
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `whether the charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year`)
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `a note of a required steps notice and of the date on which it was served`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the previous registered names`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `the details or statement that must be entered under an Order under Article 13(9)(c)`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(3)` `other information prescribed by the Minister by Order`)
-- (c), (d).
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` `the summary of the reasons for registration, produced by the charity`
#ASSERT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` `another element prescribed by an Order under Article 9(1)(d)`
-- No item of the historic section is a public element of the RESTRICTED section.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(5)` `the entity's former registered number`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` (`an item required by Article 8(5)` `a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered`)

§§ `Article 9(2): who may request entry in the restricted section`

`an entity not on the register` MEANS `an entity called` "Nobody Yet" `standing as` `not on the register` `and falling within` (LIST `a company`)

GIVEN e IS AN Entity
      funding IS A BOOLEAN
      other IS A BOOLEAN
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`may request, asked of` e `with the funding condition` funding `and another condition` other `on the readings` interp MEANS
    `Art 9(2) the request for entry in the restricted section may be made` interp e funding other

-- An applicant: the funding condition (a), or another condition (b), either suffices.
#ASSERT `may request, asked of` `a company that applies` `with the funding condition` TRUE `and another condition` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `may request, asked of` `a company that applies` `with the funding condition` FALSE `and another condition` TRUE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `may request, asked of` `a company that applies` `with the funding condition` TRUE `and another condition` TRUE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `may request, asked of` `a company that applies` `with the funding condition` FALSE `and another condition` FALSE `on the readings` fav
-- A charity registered in the general section: F3.12, the favoured reading lets it meet the condition like an applicant.
#ASSERT `may request, asked of` `a company in the general section` `with the funding condition` TRUE `and another condition` FALSE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT `may request, asked of` `a company in the general section` `with the funding condition` FALSE `and another condition` TRUE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `may request, asked of` `a company in the general section` `with the funding condition` FALSE `and another condition` FALSE `on the readings` fav
-- F3.12 other reading: "the applicant" is the entity applying to be registered, so a charity already registered can meet neither condition.
#ASSERT NOT `may request, asked of` `a company in the general section` `with the funding condition` TRUE `and another condition` FALSE `on the readings` `interpretation F3.12 reading B`
#ASSERT NOT `may request, asked of` `a company in the general section` `with the funding condition` FALSE `and another condition` TRUE `on the readings` `interpretation F3.12 reading B`
#ASSERT NOT `may request, asked of` `a company in the general section` `with the funding condition` TRUE `and another condition` TRUE `on the readings` `interpretation F3.12 reading B`
-- The applicant is unaffected by F3.12.
#ASSERT `may request, asked of` `a company that applies` `with the funding condition` TRUE `and another condition` FALSE `on the readings` `interpretation F3.12 reading B`
#ASSERT NOT `may request, asked of` `a company that applies` `with the funding condition` FALSE `and another condition` FALSE `on the readings` `interpretation F3.12 reading B`
-- Neither an applicant nor in the general section: a charity already in the restricted section, a formerly registered entity, an entity not on the register.
#ASSERT NOT `may request, asked of` `a company in the restricted section` `with the funding condition` TRUE `and another condition` TRUE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `may request, asked of` `a company, formerly registered` `with the funding condition` TRUE `and another condition` TRUE `on the readings` fav
#ASSERT NOT `may request, asked of` `an entity not on the register` `with the funding condition` TRUE `and another condition` TRUE `on the readings` fav

§§ `Article 9(3): what the Order must contain`

GIVEN grounds IS A BOOLEAN
      soliciting IS A BOOLEAN
      donation IS A BOOLEAN
      persons IS A BOOLEAN
      publicSpecified IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Content of an Order under Article 9`
`an Order with grounds` grounds `, soliciting` soliciting `, a donation` donation `, a description of persons` persons `, the general public` publicSpecified MEANS
    `Content of an Order under Article 9` WITH
        `prescribes grounds on which the Commissioner may accept or refuse a request` IS grounds
        `specifies what constitutes soliciting` IS soliciting
        `specifies what constitutes a donation` IS donation
        `prescribes a description of persons` IS persons
        `specifies what constitutes the general public` IS publicSpecified

-- Everything, with the general public specified and no description of persons: contains what the Article requires.
#ASSERT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`an Order with grounds` TRUE `, soliciting` TRUE `, a donation` TRUE `, a description of persons` FALSE `, the general public` TRUE)
-- Each of (a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) missing on its own.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`an Order with grounds` FALSE `, soliciting` TRUE `, a donation` TRUE `, a description of persons` FALSE `, the general public` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`an Order with grounds` TRUE `, soliciting` FALSE `, a donation` TRUE `, a description of persons` FALSE `, the general public` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`an Order with grounds` TRUE `, soliciting` TRUE `, a donation` FALSE `, a description of persons` FALSE `, the general public` TRUE)
-- (b)(iii): required only if the Order prescribes no description of persons.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`an Order with grounds` TRUE `, soliciting` TRUE `, a donation` TRUE `, a description of persons` FALSE `, the general public` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`an Order with grounds` TRUE `, soliciting` TRUE `, a donation` TRUE `, a description of persons` TRUE `, the general public` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`an Order with grounds` TRUE `, soliciting` TRUE `, a donation` TRUE `, a description of persons` TRUE `, the general public` TRUE)
-- A prescribed description of persons does not excuse (a), (b)(i) or (b)(ii).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`an Order with grounds` FALSE `, soliciting` TRUE `, a donation` TRUE `, a description of persons` TRUE `, the general public` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`an Order with grounds` TRUE `, soliciting` FALSE `, a donation` TRUE `, a description of persons` TRUE `, the general public` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` (`an Order with grounds` TRUE `, soliciting` TRUE `, a donation` FALSE `, a description of persons` TRUE `, the general public` FALSE)
-- The paragraphs one by one.
#ASSERT `Art 9(3)(a) the Order prescribes grounds on which the Commissioner may accept or refuse a request` (`an Order with grounds` TRUE `, soliciting` FALSE `, a donation` FALSE `, a description of persons` FALSE `, the general public` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(3)(a) the Order prescribes grounds on which the Commissioner may accept or refuse a request` (`an Order with grounds` FALSE `, soliciting` TRUE `, a donation` TRUE `, a description of persons` TRUE `, the general public` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 9(3)(b)(i) the Order specifies what constitutes soliciting` (`an Order with grounds` FALSE `, soliciting` TRUE `, a donation` FALSE `, a description of persons` FALSE `, the general public` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(3)(b)(i) the Order specifies what constitutes soliciting` (`an Order with grounds` TRUE `, soliciting` FALSE `, a donation` TRUE `, a description of persons` TRUE `, the general public` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 9(3)(b)(ii) the Order specifies what constitutes a donation` (`an Order with grounds` FALSE `, soliciting` FALSE `, a donation` TRUE `, a description of persons` FALSE `, the general public` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(3)(b)(ii) the Order specifies what constitutes a donation` (`an Order with grounds` TRUE `, soliciting` TRUE `, a donation` FALSE `, a description of persons` TRUE `, the general public` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 9(3)(b)(iii) the Order specifies what constitutes the general public, where it prescribes no description of persons` (`an Order with grounds` FALSE `, soliciting` FALSE `, a donation` FALSE `, a description of persons` FALSE `, the general public` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 9(3)(b)(iii) the Order specifies what constitutes the general public, where it prescribes no description of persons` (`an Order with grounds` FALSE `, soliciting` FALSE `, a donation` FALSE `, a description of persons` TRUE `, the general public` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(3)(b)(iii) the Order specifies what constitutes the general public, where it prescribes no description of persons` (`an Order with grounds` TRUE `, soliciting` TRUE `, a donation` TRUE `, a description of persons` FALSE `, the general public` FALSE)
-- (c): a provision of either manner is permitted.
#ASSERT `Art 9(3)(c) a provision under sub-paragraph (b) of that manner is permitted` TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 9(3)(c) a provision under sub-paragraph (b) of that manner is permitted` FALSE

§§ `Article 9(4) and (5): the request`

GIVEN published IS A BOOLEAN
      supported IS A BOOLEAN
      intention IS A MAYBE `Intention stated with a request (Article 9(5))`
GIVETH A `Request for entry in the restricted section (Article 9)`
`a request in the published form` published `, supported` supported `, with the intention` intention MEANS
    `Request for entry in the restricted section (Article 9)` WITH
        `made in the form published by the Commissioner` IS published
        `supported by information and evidence to the satisfaction of the Commissioner` IS supported
        `accompanied by a statement of the intention` IS intention

`intention (a)(i)` MEANS `that the application should be treated as withdrawn`
`intention (a)(ii)` MEANS `that the application should be treated as an application for entry in the general section, on provision of any further information and evidence required`
`intention (b)(i)` MEANS `that the charity should remain so registered`
`intention (b)(ii)` MEANS `that the charity should be treated as applying to be deregistered, on provision of any further information and evidence required`

-- 9(4): both limbs.
#ASSERT `Art 9(4) the request is in the published form and supported to the Commissioner's satisfaction` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(4) the request is in the published form and supported to the Commissioner's satisfaction` (`a request in the published form` FALSE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(4) the request is in the published form and supported to the Commissioner's satisfaction` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` FALSE `, with the intention` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(4) the request is in the published form and supported to the Commissioner's satisfaction` (`a request in the published form` FALSE `, supported` FALSE `, with the intention` NOTHING)

-- 9(5)(a): an application states (a)(i) or (a)(ii).
#ASSERT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `a company that applies` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` (JUST `intention (a)(i)`))
#ASSERT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `a company that applies` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` (JUST `intention (a)(ii)`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `a company that applies` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` (JUST `intention (b)(i)`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `a company that applies` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` (JUST `intention (b)(ii)`))
-- 9(5)(b): a charity in the general section states (b)(i) or (b)(ii).
#ASSERT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `a company in the general section` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` (JUST `intention (b)(i)`))
#ASSERT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `a company in the general section` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` (JUST `intention (b)(ii)`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `a company in the general section` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` (JUST `intention (a)(i)`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `a company in the general section` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` (JUST `intention (a)(ii)`))
-- No statement at all.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `a company that applies` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `a company in the general section` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` NOTHING)
-- Not an applicant or a general-section charity: no statement fits.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `a company in the restricted section` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` (JUST `intention (b)(i)`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `a company, formerly registered` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` (JUST `intention (a)(i)`))
-- 9(6)(a)'s fact: complied with both paragraphs.
#ASSERT `Art 9(4) and (5) the request complied` `a company that applies` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` (JUST `intention (a)(ii)`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(4) and (5) the request complied` `a company that applies` (`a request in the published form` FALSE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` (JUST `intention (a)(ii)`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(4) and (5) the request complied` `a company that applies` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` (JUST `intention (b)(ii)`))
#ASSERT `Art 9(4) and (5) the request complied` `a company in the general section` (`a request in the published form` TRUE `, supported` TRUE `, with the intention` (JUST `intention (b)(ii)`))

§§ `Article 9(6): when the Commissioner may enter the charity`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Satisfaction of the Commissioner under Article 9(6)`
`the Commissioner is satisfied of (a)` a `, of (b)` b `, of (c)` c MEANS
    `Satisfaction of the Commissioner under Article 9(6)` WITH
        `satisfied that the request complied with paragraphs (4) and (5)` IS a
        `satisfied that one of the conditions prescribed under paragraph (2) is met` IS b
        `satisfied that there is no ground on which the request must be refused or, for a discretionary ground, should be refused` IS c

-- All eight combinations: only all three satisfactions allow the entry.
#ASSERT `Art 9(6) the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section` (`the Commissioner is satisfied of (a)` TRUE `, of (b)` TRUE `, of (c)` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6) the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section` (`the Commissioner is satisfied of (a)` FALSE `, of (b)` TRUE `, of (c)` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6) the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section` (`the Commissioner is satisfied of (a)` TRUE `, of (b)` FALSE `, of (c)` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6) the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section` (`the Commissioner is satisfied of (a)` TRUE `, of (b)` TRUE `, of (c)` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6) the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section` (`the Commissioner is satisfied of (a)` FALSE `, of (b)` FALSE `, of (c)` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6) the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section` (`the Commissioner is satisfied of (a)` FALSE `, of (b)` TRUE `, of (c)` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6) the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section` (`the Commissioner is satisfied of (a)` TRUE `, of (b)` FALSE `, of (c)` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6) the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section` (`the Commissioner is satisfied of (a)` FALSE `, of (b)` FALSE `, of (c)` FALSE)

-- (c): no mandatory ground applies and the Commissioner does not consider refusal right on a discretionary ground.
#ASSERT `Art 9(6)(c) there is no ground on which the request must be refused or should be refused` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6)(c) there is no ground on which the request must be refused or should be refused` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6)(c) there is no ground on which the request must be refused or should be refused` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 9(6)(c) there is no ground on which the request must be refused or should be refused` TRUE TRUE

-- The prohibition: an entry made without all three satisfactions is a breach; with all three, nothing was prohibited.
-- EXPECT: BREACH | entered the charity in the restricted section without being satisfied
#TRACE `Art 9(6) the Commissioner must not enter the charity in the restricted section unless satisfied` (`the Commissioner is satisfied of (a)` TRUE `, of (b)` FALSE `, of (c)` TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter a charity in the restricted section of the register` AT 5

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 9(6) the Commissioner must not enter the charity in the restricted section unless satisfied` (`the Commissioner is satisfied of (a)` TRUE `, of (b)` TRUE `, of (c)` TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter a charity in the restricted section of the register` AT 5

-- Not satisfied and no entry made: the prohibition stands (it has no end).
-- EXPECT: STANDING | MUST NOT `enter a charity in the restricted section of the register`
#TRACE `Art 9(6) the Commissioner must not enter the charity in the restricted section unless satisfied` (`the Commissioner is satisfied of (a)` FALSE `, of (b)` FALSE `, of (c)` FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- The decision of the Commissioner (IP27).
#ASSERT `Art 9(6) the decision of the Commissioner on the request for the restricted section` TRUE EQUALS `Decision of the Commissioner` WITH subject IS `whether to enter a charity in the restricted section, Article 9(6) and (7)`, outcome IS `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
#ASSERT `Art 9(6) the decision of the Commissioner on the request for the restricted section` FALSE EQUALS `Decision of the Commissioner` WITH subject IS `whether to enter a charity in the restricted section, Article 9(6) and (7)`, outcome IS `the Commissioner refuses`

§§ `Article 9(7): a refusal`

-- (a): written notice, with no time stated.  Refused, notice given: discharged.  Refused and nothing done however long: the duty stands -- there is no deadline to breach.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 9(7)(a) the Commissioner must give written notice of the refusal` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give written notice of the refusal of a request` AT 400

-- EXPECT: STANDING | MUST `give written notice of the refusal of a request`
#TRACE `Art 9(7)(a) the Commissioner must give written notice of the refusal` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- Not refused: no notice owed.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
